Adapt the Poly1305 calls to crypton >= 2.0, where Poly1305.auth and
Poly1305.initialize take an opaque Poly1305.Key built by Poly1305.key
rather than the raw key bytes.  The key material generated by xSalsa20
is always 32 bytes, so building the key cannot fail.

Index: src/Simplex/Messaging/Crypto/Lazy.hs
--- src/Simplex/Messaging/Crypto/Lazy.hs.orig
+++ src/Simplex/Messaging/Crypto/Lazy.hs
@@ -208,7 +208,7 @@
 {-# INLINE kcbInit #-}
 
 sbInit_ :: ByteArrayAccess key => key -> ByteString -> Either CryptoError SbState
-sbInit_ secret nonce = (state2,) <$> cryptoPassed (Poly1305.initialize rs)
+sbInit_ secret nonce = (state2,) . Poly1305.initialize <$> cryptoPassed (Poly1305.key rs)
   where
     zero = B.replicate 16 $ toEnum 0
     (iv0, iv1) = B.splitAt 8 nonce
